This file marks the CRAFT framework's own repository.

Its presence means:
  - `framework/` is the work, not read-only reference
  - `craft.py manifest`, `gates`, `release` and `init` will run
  - `verify` does not warn that framework files have been modified

Its absence means this is a project using the framework, where the reverse
holds on every point.

`python3 framework/craft.py init` deletes this file, which is what turns a
clone of the framework into a project. It lives at the repository root rather
than inside `framework/` so that `craft.py upgrade`, which copies only
`framework/`, can never carry it into a project.

Do not delete it by hand in the framework repository.
